- **SUBJ-R2** — The whole somatic frame ("What Cara Delevingne's body kept saying for her," "Her body had been filing reports for twenty-three years") recasts what she described as deliberate self-harm as her body acting without her. I pulled the verbatim from the draft's own transcript source: *"I also just started throwing myself off stuff… Because I was in pain inside, but I didn't know how to express it. So I just wanted to feel pain."* The draft quotes the middle clause and drops both the act and the motive. Critically, the fix strengthens the thesis — the draft's own tie-breaker, "a bid to be witnessed," is the accurate frame, and a deliberate bid is far better Type 4 evidence than an involuntary symptom, because symptoms have no motive.

**Strongest hit:** the voice reframe at L227–231 — "the four careers are one request, refused three times and repeated anyway" — built entirely from her vocabulary and applied to the behavior she's most mocked for. That's the piece's dignity engine; preserve intact.

**Highest-priority concern (SUBJ-C1):** L223's "Nobody handed her the Warner contract on a blind listen" is an unsourced factual claim about how she got a record deal, conceded on her behalf. She has an on-record concession of her own that's better and fairer — the Vogue 2023 "she's spoiled, there's nepotism… which I did, don't get me wrong. But life wasn't all that easy for other reasons." Swapping it fixes the sourcing and strengthens the concession.

